`{!loading && <TaskCounts .../>}` \u2192 `{false && ...}`), reran just the count-related tests \u2192 **all 8 failed** with real assertion diffs (proving they exercise real behavior, not vacuous). Restored the line, reran full suite \u2192 **38 passed** again.\n7. Ran the backend suite as a regression check even though this is frontend-only: `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 **35 passed**, confirming backend is untouched and healthy, matching both docs' \"no backend change\" non-goal.\n8. Ran `npm run build` \u2192 succeeded, no type/build errors.\n\n**Not independently verified live:** criterion 9 (fetch error on initial load shouldn't crash or blank the count). I drafted a 9th e2e test for this but the edit was denied by the permission system, and follow-up `git`/bash checks were also denied \u2014 I stopped retrying rather than loop on refusals. Verified instead by code trace: `App.jsx`'s `refresh()` only clears `tasks` on success (`setTasks(await api.listTasks())`), never on the `catch` branch, and `loading` is cleared in `finally` regardless of outcome \u2014 so `TaskCounts` (gated only on `!loading`) keeps rendering the last-known `tasks` state (`0/0` on a first-load failure) with no crash path. This is a straightforward read of the code, not a live-browser observation, so I'm flagging it as an explicit gap rather than a pass.\n\nNo defects found. All 8 criteria with live browser coverage pass; the 9th is sound by code inspection but unverified live in this session.\n\nVERDICT: pass", "meta": {"native_type": "result", "subtype": "success", "session_id": "a1a9fb2d-6eda-4780-a0e2-d3742e9e5fcd", "is_error": false, "total_cost_usd": 1.2561816000000001}}
